        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Concepts: Dysteleology, science-oriented atheism\n- People: Ernst Haeckel, Richard Dawkins, Sam Harris, Christopher Hitchens\n- Publications: New Statesman, The Nation, The Weekly Standard, The Atlantic, London Review of Books, The Times Literary Supplement, Slate, Free Inquiry, Vanity Fair\n\nFacts:\n- Dysteleology is an aggressive but optimistic form of science-oriented atheism.\n- Dysteleology was originally perhaps associated with Ernst Haeckel and his followers.\n- Dysteleology is now perhaps more associated with the atheism of Richard Dawkins, Sam Harris, and Christopher Hitchens.\n- Christopher Hitchens contributed to New Statesman, The Nation, The Weekly Standard, The Atlantic, London Review of Books, The Times Literary Supplement, Slate, Free Inquiry, and Vanity Fair.",
